  "domain": "infrastructure",
  "definition": "An integrated circuit (IC) is a set of electronic circuits \u2014 transistors, resistors, capacitors and their interconnections \u2014 fabricated as a single monolithic device on a wafer of semiconductor material, usually silicon. By miniaturising and mass-producing complete circuits photolithographically, ICs made computation cheap, fast and reliable, enabling microprocessors, memory, FPGAs and application-specific chips; transistor density doubled roughly every two years in the trend described by Moore's Law, underpinning the whole of modern digital infrastructure.",
